    - analysis_quality  # 5a68
    isbefore: []  # 5a68
    duplicate_of: []  # 5a68
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 5a68
    pr_ref:  # 5a68
    description: "FOUND 2026-10-01 measuring WI-saduj (residual: same symptom, different cause). After WI-saduj's declarator walk, the c/cpp function definitions still left WITHOUT a symbol on the measured repos are all definitions whose name comes from a MACRO tree-sitter cannot expand. Calls inside them are left unemitted (by design since #1237: they are not anchored on the file).\n\nMeasured (instrument: every call_expression/new_expression whose innermost tree-sitter function_definition has no analyzer symbol at its position; ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_09302026/saduj/measure.py, after2.* outputs):\n  redis (c):  2598 call sites in defs shaped `parenthesized_declarator>identifier` -- jemalloc's test macro `TEST_BEGIN(test_x) { ... }`; 210 sites in defs whose declarator is a bare `identifier` -- deps/fast_float/fast_float.h, a C++ header the C grammar parses (redis has no C++ file, so header_owner gives .h to C).\n  tmate (c):  26 sites, `pointer_declarator>identifier`, compat/tree.h (RB_GENERATE-style macro bodies).\n  x265 / redis: `PFX(name)(args)` and `LUALIB_API int (f) (args)` parse as a function_declarator directly inside another. WI-saduj deliberately leaves these unnamed rather than mint symbols called `PFX` or `int` (test_c_call_anchor::test_a_macro_named_definition_mints_no_symbol).\n  sherpa-onnx (cpp): `class SHERPA_ONNX_API X : public MoveOnly<X, Y> {..}` parses as a function_definition whose declarator is the template `MoveOnly<..>`; the class and its methods get no symbols at all (also deliberately not named by WI-saduj).\n  crun, bento4, modsecurity, falco: 0 remaining.\n\nNot decided here: whether to name such a definition (the macro ARGUMENT is the real name for TEST_BEGIN and PFX; for the export-macro class, the fix is the parse, not the name -- cf. WI-gafip for objc's argument-less attribute macros). Priority P3: the sites are concentrated in vendored test code (jemalloc tests) and one header misparse."  # 5a68
    fields: {}  # 5a68
- op: discuss  # e461
  at: '2026-10-04T22:59:14Z'  # e461
  by: agent  # e461
  actor: jgstern_agent  # e461
  clock: 2  # e461
  nonce: e461  # e461
  message: "Branch jgstern-agent/fix/darik, commits 80ecd183ca (edge_source) and c7c31f7676 (c, cpp). NOT merged, no status change.\n\nDecision taken (per the owner's brief): no name is invented for a macro-named definition. Every edge drawn from inside one -- c: calls, callback-argument calls, &f references, dispatch-table uses; cpp: every edge of the walk -- comes from the nearest enclosing record with a symbol (an outer definition, else the file anchor) and carries meta.src_stands_in_for = \"unnamed_definition\" (registered edge_meta key, per call site, single writer: edge_source.mark_stand_in). Before, those calls were left unemitted, or, inside a NAMED outer definition, silently drawn from it.\n\nMeasured (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_10032026/darik/{base,after1}.{c,cpp}.*.json): redis 2,816 of 2,823 call sites in unnamed definitions now have an edge (2,985 calls + 54 references edges, all from the file, all marked); tmate 26 of 26 (compat/tree.h RB_* macro bodies); x265 1 of 1 (x265::cpu_detect, a real call); sherpa-onnx 3 edges, ALL THREE parse artifacts of the export-macro class misparse (an \"if (...)\" read as a call to if, two \"X() = default\"). crun, falco, bento4, modsecurity: 0. Read samples: 12 random redis stand-ins are real calls in jemalloc TEST_BEGIN bodies; 12 tmate ones are real macro uses.\n\nNot done: the export-macro class misparse itself -- filed WI-divus-garom-zojav-golog-sidod-hibit-kavit-tozij. Also found with the new gate: c.py's dispatch-table VARIABLE is never emitted, so dispatches_to srcs dangle (crun 94, redis 505, tmate 129; unchanged by this branch) -- filed WI-dirij-norod-pugup-sasoh-satab-lubut-tahap-jupuz."  # e461
